## Same change set

When you change a command, its reply, a hook name or signature, paging, storage layout, install, or a config constant, update the owning doc in the same commit. Clarifications found while answering questions belong in the doc too.

## Current behavior only

Describe how it works today. Do not write "used to", "previously", "no longer", "legacy", "replaced", or before/after comparisons in the guides or internals. Delete the stale sentence and write the current one.

History belongs in [CHANGELOG.md](../../src/modules/LoBBS/CHANGELOG.md) and the commit message.

## Succinct

One home per fact. Link instead of repeating a table. Put exact constants once, in internals.

## Voice

Root README intro for tone. Style rules: `meshenvy.org/.cursor/skills/blog-voice/SKILL.md`. User guides speak to "you". No closing recap paragraphs, no em dashes, no semicolons joining sentences, no bold in prose.
